# No trailing slashes: a pattern ending in `/` matches a directory only, and a
# symlink is not one. A worktree that links `node_modules`, `data` or `rules`
# back to the main checkout — which is the only way to work in one — then has
# those links staged by `git add -A`. Without the slash both the directory and
# a link to it are ignored.

# build / tooling
node_modules
.claude/worktrees

# credentials. Nothing in the repo carries key material any more — SB1 signs
# nothing and the refresh token lives in the macOS keychain — so these globs
# guard against one ever landing loose rather than covering a directory of them.
*.pem
*.key
.env*

# personal data: raw API responses, the derived database, the dashboard
data

# hand-edited local rules — they carry account keys, names and descriptions
rules

# a tfvars file holds every secret in the clear, and so does a saved plan.
# The state itself lives in Azure, not here.
infra/.terraform
infra/*.tfstate*
infra/tfplan
*.tfplan
*.tfvars
